# (2) Dickson's conditional constant of boric acid in seawater: pK*B = 8.5975 on the total scale
#     (S 35, 25 C; Dickson, Deep-Sea Res. 37 (1990) 755 -- the primary was NOT read here; the number is
#     the one evaluated in docs/design/boron-in-seawater-apparent-pka-study.md section 4), moved to the
#     free scale on molality: pK*F = 8.6896.  At the GIVEN pH 8.2 the engine's m_H (8.5737e-9) and the
#     total boron 4.3116e-4 turn that constant into the free boric acid it implies:
#         R = 10^-8.6896 / m_H = 0.23836 ,  m_H3BO3 = 4.3116e-4 / (1 + R) = 3.4817e-4 mol/kg.
#     The model gives 3.4614e-4 (pK*F 8.6765, 0.013 below Dickson).  PARTLY INDEPENDENT: the seawater
#     measurement is not in the paper's fit, but the paper's Na/Ca/Mg borate terms were fitted to the
#     emf data of the same laboratory family (Hershey et al. 1985; Dickson, unpublished, for K).
#     The gap equals the error of the scale conversion (about 0.01 in pK) to within a factor of two.
